    "oracles": {
      "note": "Locked on 2026-11-20 before the first recording of this campaign; never loosened after a result (a run that disagrees is a finding). 'available' means the metric must be available; a reason code means it must be unavailable with exactly that reason; 'either' is no prediction (the run records which). Basis, all from facts known before the recording: (1) sizes: a 1-DOF model of each joint (the inertia the worker reads back at the bench pose with no step run: J1 0.352, J2 0.584, J3 0.713, J4 0.113, J5 0.136, J6 0.101, gripper 0.00232 kg m2; the starting kp/kd; the effort limit; the MuJoCo position actuator kp(r-q)-kv*qdot) predicts a peak speed under the OVERSPEED trip (1.2 x 3.14 rad/s; gripper 1.2 x 10) for every 0.05 rad step (at most 2.2 rad/s, J5) and every 0.1 rad trapezoid at 0.5 rad/s, 2 rad/s2 (at most 0.45 rad/s), while J4 and J5 trip at 0.1 rad and every joint at 0.2 rad; the same model gives J3: 0.1 completes and 0.2 trips, as V06c/V07a measured. J2 steps the way V06c ran it (negative). (2) Metrics: a trapezoid's step metrics are SIGNAL_NOT_STEP by definition (bench-runner benchMetrics); the wheel step repeats the V06c result of this plant and profile (P-only speed loop: steady-state error 0.066 rad/s, above the 2 % band, so settlingTimeS NOT_SETTLED); joints J1-J5 settle inside the 2 % band (their joint frictionloss of 1 N m over kp leaves at most 0.0005 rad, under 0.001 rad = 2 % of 0.05); J6's frictionloss deadband (1/500 = 0.002 rad) is wider than that band, and the gripper's mimic joints have no friction but unknown passive loads, so their settling time is no prediction. Every completed run: the trace covers ticks 0-500 complete (5,000 samples per axis, 11 chunks), and the gain suggestions equal gainSuggestions of the inertia the run reports.",
